@@ -45,6 +45,19 @@ Any dictionaries that you pass to a request method will be merged with the
 session-level values that are set. The method-level parameters override session
 parameters.
 
+You can set a default :ref:`timeout <timeouts>` for a session::
+
+    s = requests.Session(timeout=(3.05, 10))
+    s.get('https://httpbin.org/get')  # uses the session timeout
+    s.get('https://httpbin.org/get', timeout=5)  # overrides it for this request
+    s.get('https://httpbin.org/get', timeout=None)  # disables the timeout
+    s.timeout = 20  # changes the default for subsequent requests
+
+The default is ``None``, meaning no timeout. Requests that omit ``timeout`` use
+the current ``s.timeout``, including calls to ``s.send`` with a prepared request.
+Every redirect uses the timeout selected for the initial request. Per-request
+overrides leave ``s.timeout`` unchanged.
+
 Note, however, that method-level parameters will *not* be persisted across
 requests, even if using a session. This example will only send the cookies
 with the first request, but not the second::
